robin <usenet@unrated.net> wrote:
>
> I'm happy to see any new roguelike games developed, regardless of how
> much narrative or mechanics they borrow from pre-existing games, but I
> think it'd be reasonable to object to (and even shun) a new project
> that tried to take on the name of a pre-existing game.

There have been a lot of NetHack variants that appended something to
NetHack (like NetHack Brass or NetHack Plus).

What's your opinion about that?

> The /dev/null/nethack Tournament is a _NetHack_ tournament and will
> always be run on vanilla NetHack; much as we may like to add content
> around the vanilla core, that material will always be secondary to the
> central tournament.

It seems this also applies to bug fixes for known crashes of the
vanilla code base.

What's the reason for this?

> We'd be happy to have other roguelike's involved
> (like we did with ZAPM this year, or as adjuncts to the main
> tournament in some other way) or to help folks set up new tournaments
> for other roguelikes, and if/when NeoHack is ready we'd be just as
> happy to involve it this way as well.

As far as I am concerned, your addition of ZAPM was a huge success.

Going for the most unique deaths in ZAPM took so much time that I only
got the Plastic Star in NetHack. :D

